From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Tue, 25 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: split PLAYER_NONE and PLAYER_ALL from duelist seats 2
 and 3

With 3 or 4 duelists, seats 2 and 3 have the numbers of PLAYER_NONE (2) and PLAYER_ALL (3). So
every card and effect of seat 2 was treated as "no controller". This patch adds field::none_id()
and field::all_id(). They return PLAYER_NONE and PLAYER_ALL when n_duelists is 2, and DUELIST_NONE
(0xFF) and DUELIST_ALL (0xFE) otherwise. It also adds field::reset_sentinels().

Changes, all on the same line as the stock text (token substitution):
- Changed lines: card.cpp 11, effect.cpp 4, field.cpp 7, operations.cpp 40, processor.cpp 41,
  libcard.cpp 14, libduel.cpp 30: a write of the sentinel, or a compare with it, now uses none_id()
  or all_id(). lua_get defaults now use the runtime default overload. The checks "playerid >
  PLAYER_NONE" and "IsEnvironment" become is_duelist(p) or p == none_id()/all_id() (same set at n == 2).
- Default initializers (card owner and controler, effect owner, BattleCommand reason_player, field
  reason_player, conti_player, nil_event) are set again after the duel size is known: the card
  constructor, duel::new_effect, one else line in the battle damage step, and reset_sentinels() called
  at the end of Debug.SetupDuelists.

With 2 duelists the helpers return the stock values, so every byte and every branch is unchanged.

Left alone: values that come straight from Lua (SetOperationInfo op_player, Duel.Win, chkf, SetReasonPlayer,
RockPaperScissors result): the phase 3 fold translates them. The win and loss blocks (winp) belong to T5A.
The count-map key with PLAYER_NONE (effect.cpp) is only a key. Sites are listed in sites.tsv.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UrYy4jjEcbJHKdcVYasfdb
